@*
 * FILE ROLE: Applied automatically to every .cshtml in this Views/ folder
 *            (and all sub-folders) before the view itself is compiled.
 *            Declares global @using namespaces and enables Tag Helpers so
 *            individual view files stay lean.
 *
 * SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
 *   1. @using directives  — namespaces available in all views without repeating
 *   2. @addTagHelper      — enabling Tag Helpers from an assembly
 *
 * HOW _ViewImports.cshtml WORKS:
 *   The Razor engine walks UP the folder tree from the view being rendered
 *   and applies every _ViewImports.cshtml it finds (innermost wins for
 *   conflicting @namespace declarations). This means:
 *     Views/_ViewImports.cshtml     → applied to ALL views
 *     Views/Demo/_ViewImports.cshtml → applied only to Views/Demo/*.cshtml
 *   This chapter uses a single root-level file for simplicity.
 *
 * WHAT BELONGS HERE vs IN A VIEW FILE:
 *   _ViewImports.cshtml  — namespaces used across many views, Tag Helper assemblies
 *   Individual view      — @using for one-off types; @model; per-view @inject
 *
 * DIRECTIVES ALLOWED IN _ViewImports.cshtml:
 *   @using, @inject, @model, @inherits, @addTagHelper, @removeTagHelper, @namespace
 *   NOT allowed: @{ } code blocks, HTML output, @functions
 *@

@*
 * SECTION 1: @using DIRECTIVES
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every @using here is equivalent to writing the same @using at the top of
 * every .cshtml file in the project. With ImplicitUsings disabled in .csproj,
 * these must be declared explicitly.
 *
 *   ViewsRazorSyntax.Models  — makes ArticleViewModel accessible as just
 *                              "ArticleViewModel" without the full namespace
 *   Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering — IHtmlHelper<T>, SelectList used by
 *                              @Html.* helper methods
 *@
@using ViewsRazorSyntax.Models
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering

@*
 * SECTION 2: @addTagHelper DIRECTIVE
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Tag Helpers are C# classes that augment HTML elements with server-side
 * behaviour by processing matching attributes (asp-action, asp-controller, etc.).
 *
 * SYNTAX:
 *   @addTagHelper *, AssemblyName
 *     * — wildcard: enable ALL Tag Helpers in the assembly
 *
 *   @addTagHelper Fully.Qualified.TagHelperClass, AssemblyName
 *     — enable a single Tag Helper class
 *
 *   @removeTagHelper *, AssemblyName   — disable all in an assembly
 *   @removeTagHelper Name, Assembly    — disable one specifically
 *
 * Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers ships with ASP.NET Core and provides:
 *   <form asp-action>  <input asp-for>  <a asp-action asp-controller>
 *   <label asp-for>    <span asp-validation-for>  <select asp-for>  etc.
 *
 * PREVIEW — Full Tag Helper depth is in → 08. Tag Helpers
 *
 * Without this line, those asp-* attributes are treated as plain HTML
 * attributes and the server-side processing never runs.
 *@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
